Asset: {{asset}}
Muse directions:
{{context | default("Run design_muse first; report missing handoff.")}}

Read `v3/creative-spec.md` (palette law, contour language, animation language), `v3/script.md` (the asset's job) and `v3/rubric.md` (C1–C19). Build one sprite component per muse direction (3 or more) under {{files}}, each a five-role flat SVG with a pale contour, designed shadow shapes and 2–3 boil variants, fills by role never hex. Each variant's label names the reference properties it borrows (by file in `v3/references/` and the property, e.g. 'Seuss cat-stairway: elongated neck, flowing hair mass') and the existing cast property it sits between (e.g. 'Clawd's block mass and Codex's cloud lobes'). Register the variants in an `AssetSheet` composition and render one still at frame 0. Do not pick; the owner picks from the still. Losers remain as controls, not deleted.

Return: Variants (id, title, borrows, between, file); Sheet Path; What Was Held Constant; Concerns.
